# Symptom Tracker copy style

Applies to UI labels, help text, FAQs, PDF export copy, onboarding, and marketing.

## No em dashes

Do not use `—` or `–` as punctuation in user-facing copy.

Prefer periods, commas, colons, or parentheses.

## Avoid AI buzzword tone

Do not use hype words unless technically required: AI-assisted, AI-powered, leverage, seamlessly, unlock, streamline, harness, cutting-edge, game-changer, empower, delve, robust, innovative, utilize.

Prefer plain verbs: organize, use, help, may, sometimes, can, often.

When describing uncertain outcomes, prefer **may** or **sometimes** over definitive claims.

## OK to keep

- Code comments and internal developer strings
- Product names (Symptom Tracker Pro)
